  "question": {
    "text": "Given below are two statements :<br/>Statement (I) : The dimensions of Planck's constant and angular momentum are same.<br/>Statement (II) : In Bohr's model electron revolve around the nucleus only in those orbits for which angular momentum is integral multiple of Planck's constant.<br/>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "OD93K",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "paxdm",
      "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XZe2T",
      "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "kL6lW",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{E}=\\mathrm{hf} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{ML}^2 \\mathrm{~T}^{-2}=[\\mathrm{h}] \\times\\left[\\mathrm{T}^{-1}\\right] \\\\\n& {[\\mathrm{h}]=\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^2 \\mathrm{~T}^{-1}\\right]} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{L}=[\\mathrm{MVR}]=\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^2 \\mathrm{~T}^{-1}\\right] \\\\\n& \\mathrm{L}=\\frac{\\mathrm{nh}}{2 \\pi}<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>L is integral multiple of $\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2 \\pi}$",
    "image": null
  },
